# 6. Frontend Technical Choices

## 6.1 Phaser Usage
Use Phaser for:
- battle maps,
- enemies and projectiles,
- animation playback,
- visual combat feedback,
- lightweight in-battle HUD.

Reason:
Phaser is designed for browser-based 2D games and supports Canvas/WebGL rendering for this type of product. [blog.logrocket](https://blog.logrocket.com/best-javascript-html5-game-engines-2025/)

## 6.2 React Usage
Use React for:
- inventory lists,
- item compare panels,
- build setup screens,
- skill trees,
- missions,
- season timeline,
- settings.

Reason:
These screens behave more like application panels than real-time gameplay, and React is a better fit for structured form/state interaction. [linkedin](https://www.linkedin.com/posts/probietech_reactjs-phaserjs-webgamedevelopment-activity-7382342476675825665-bPP9)

## 6.3 Why Not Everything in React
Avoid using React as the primary game engine.  
For combat-heavy rendering, a dedicated game layer is cleaner and more performant.

## 6.4 Vite Usage
Vite should be used for:
- dev server,
- HMR,
- production bundling,
- asset loading optimization,
- environment variable injection.

The official Phaser + Vite template supports this exact setup. [phaser](https://phaser.io/news/2024/01/phaser-vite-template)

