# 9. Game Data Architecture

## 9.1 Data-Driven Design
All major gameplay content should be data-driven:
- classes
- skills
- items
- enemies
- map nodes
- season modifiers
- missions

## 9.2 Content File Format
Recommended formats:
- JSON for runtime data.
- YAML if your team prefers human readability for design iteration.
- CSV for balancing spreadsheets.

## 9.3 Data Loading Flow
1. Client loads static game definitions.
2. Server loads authoritative content pack version.
3. Client compares version hash.
4. Mismatched definitions trigger reload or patch flow.

## 9.4 Definition Versioning
Every content table should have:
- version number,
- last updated timestamp,
- optional migration notes.

This is important for seasonal updates because the game will change every 14 days.

