# 11. Rendering and Asset Pipeline

## 11.1 Rendering Approach
Use 2D sprite-based presentation:
- sprite sheets,
- atlas textures,
- light particle effects,
- screen-space damage numbers.

## 11.2 Asset Categories
- character sprites,
- enemy sprites,
- skill VFX,
- UI icons,
- item icons,
- seasonal theme assets,
- audio assets.

## 11.3 Asset Loading Strategy
- Lazy-load battle assets only when entering battle.
- Preload UI assets for hub screens.
- Cache common atlases.
- Use progressive loading for large seasonal content.

## 11.4 Performance Budget
Keep the game lightweight:
- avoid large texture count per scene,
- avoid excessive DOM overlays during battle,
- keep particle counts controlled,
- avoid unnecessary allocations in combat ticks.

