# 12. State Management Architecture

## 12.1 State Categories
### Local transient state
- current screen,
- opened modal,
- hover state,
- current battle scene state.

### Session state
- current build preset,
- current selected map,
- temporary battle conditions.

### Persistent state
- account progression,
- inventory,
- class unlocks,
- season state.

## 12.2 State Store Strategy
Recommended approach:
- one global store for high-level app state,
- one combat store for battle runtime,
- one server sync layer for persistence.

## 12.3 State Update Rules
- Combat state updates should be isolated.
- UI state should never mutate server state directly.
- All persistent actions should go through an action service.

