# 13. API Design

## 13.1 Core Endpoints

### Auth
- `POST /auth/login`
- `POST /auth/logout`
- `GET /auth/session`

### Profile
- `GET /player/profile`
- `PATCH /player/profile`

### Character
- `GET /character/state`
- `PATCH /character/state`

### Inventory
- `GET /inventory`
- `POST /inventory/equip`
- `POST /inventory/unequip`
- `POST /inventory/discard`

### Skills
- `GET /skills/presets`
- `POST /skills/presets`
- `PATCH /skills/presets/:id`

### Idle
- `GET /idle/buildings`
- `PATCH /idle/buildings/:id/upgrade`
- `POST /idle/collect`

### Battle
- `POST /battle/start`
- `POST /battle/submit-result`
- `GET /battle/reward-summary/:id`

### Season
- `GET /season/current`
- `GET /season/progress`
- `POST /season/claim`
- `GET /season/reset-preview`

### Missions
- `GET /missions/daily`
- `GET /missions/seasonal`
- `POST /missions/claim`

### Admin
- `POST /admin/season/reset`
- `POST /admin/content/publish`

## 13.2 API Principles
- Keep payloads explicit and typed.
- Use idempotent endpoints where possible.
- Separate read and write endpoints cleanly.
- Return version hashes with content requests.

